On Mon, Jan 6, 2014 at 8:22 PM, selpa'i <seladwa@gmx.de> wrote:

>
>    lo nu broda pu cinri
>    ! "The event of brodaing in the past is interesting."
>

Actually it's even worse than that, it's just a sumti: "the brodaing in the
past type of interesting thing."

Using {cu} before {pu} is necessary there to prevent the accidental
> slipping of the {pu} into the abstraction. So maybe that's one reason to
> use {cu} even when it's not necessary: to be less likely to forget it where
> it must be used.


Yes, it's a good idea not to rely on tenses to do the job of "cu", as they
can't always do it.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

